---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ImagePlaceholder from "../../components/ImagePlaceholder.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import MailButton from "../../components/MailButton.astro";
import poohAtWork from "../../assets/images/illustrations/pooh-at-work.webp";
import { enPerson, enBreadcrumb } from "../../utils/schema-en";
import { EMAIL, EMAIL_URL, GITHUB_URL } from "../../../site.config.mjs";

const personSchema = enPerson(Astro.site);

const aboutPageSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "AboutPage",
	name: "About Purin Buriwong",
	url: new URL("/en/about/", Astro.site).href,
	mainEntity: { "@type": "Person", name: "Purin Buriwong" },
};

const breadcrumb = enBreadcrumb(Astro.site, "About", "/en/about/");

const facts: { label: string; value: string }[] = [
	{ label: "Name", value: "Purin Buriwong" },
	{ label: "Goes by", value: "Pooh" },
	{ label: "Work", value: "Freelance software developer" },
	{
		label: "Based in",
		value: "Bangkok, Thailand. Available for remote work with clients anywhere.",
	},
	{ label: "Languages", value: "Thai and English" },
	{
		label: "Education",
		value: "Computer Engineering, Mahidol University International College",
	},
	{ label: "Experience", value: "More than seven years building software" },
];

const services: { label: string; href: string }[] = [
	{ label: "Back-office and internal business systems", href: "/en/backoffice/" },
	{ label: "Business websites", href: "/en/work/" },
	{ label: "Finishing sites that were started with AI", href: "/en/fix-ai-website/" },
	{ label: "What affects the budget", href: "/en/budget-factors/" },
];
---

<Layout
	lang="en"
	title="About Purin Buriwong (Pooh), Freelance Developer in Bangkok | Pooh"
	description="Purin Buriwong, known as Pooh. Freelance software developer based in Bangkok, Thailand, building business websites and back-office systems for customers here and remotely. Seven years of experience, ex-Agoda, runs pawjai.co."
	schema={[personSchema, aboutPageSchema, breadcrumb]}
>
	<section class="page-head band-cream">
		<div class="shell page-head-inner">
			<p class="label">About me</p>
			<h1>Hello, I am Pooh. Here is a bit about how I work.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				I started writing software before AI could write code, and the thing
				that stuck with me from those years is simple:
				<strong
					>a system is not really finished on launch day. It is finished when
					someone can still change it two years later.</strong
				>
			</p>
			{/* The entity paragraph. Self-contained on purpose: quoted alone it
			    still says who he is and how to reach him, and Person.description
			    mirrors it. Full-size body copy, never fine print. */}
			<p class="entity">
				<strong
					>Purin Buriwong, who goes by Pooh, is a freelance software developer
					based in Bangkok, Thailand.</strong
				> He builds business websites and back-office systems for customers, and
				he takes remote work with clients in Thailand and abroad. He has been
				building software for more than seven years, he was on the developer
				team at Agoda, and he founded and still runs <a
					href="https://pawjai.co"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener">pawjai.co</a
				>. He works in English and Thai. Reach him by email at {EMAIL}.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="intro">
				<div class="intro-media reveal">
					<div class="photo-frame">
						<ImagePlaceholder
							src={poohAtWork}
							alt="Three dimensional illustration of the Pooh mascot working at a desk"
							label="Pooh mascot at work"
							ratio="4 / 5"
							loading="eager"
							fetchpriority="high"
							sizes="(min-width: 68rem) 22rem, (min-width: 48rem) 36vw, calc(100vw - 2.75rem)"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="intro-text reveal reveal-d1">
					<h2>The short version</h2>
					<p>
						I started writing software when there was no tool to write it for
						you. Everything had to be worked out, tried, and fixed by hand.
						That is a slow way to learn and it teaches you things that have not
						stopped being true.
					</p>
					<p>
						I spent time on the developer team at Agoda. That is where I
						learned what a system needs when a lot of real people depend on it
						and nobody can afford for it to be down.
					</p>
					<p>
						Then I started pawjai.co, a product I built and still run myself.
						When it breaks at an awkward hour, I am the one who gets up. That
						has quietly changed how I build things for other people too: I try
						not to take the shortcut that is easy today and painful in a year,
						because I have been on the wrong end of that.
					</p>
					<p>
						I use AI every day now, like most developers do. It is fast and it
						is genuinely useful.
						<strong
							>What matters is knowing which parts you can hand to it and which
							parts will cause trouble later.</strong
						>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band-tint">
		<div class="shell">
			{/* Practical answers only. An earlier draft opened this section by
			    arguing that hiring in Thailand is not a compromise, which was
			    the same thesis the home page made and made it twice. Per ADR
			    0002 that argument now appears once, on the home page, and this
			    section simply answers what someone hiring from abroad wants to
			    know. */}
			<div class="section-head reveal">
				<p class="label">Working together</p>
				<h2>If you are hiring me from another country</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="why reveal reveal-d1">
				<p>
					I am in Bangkok, Thailand, and a good part of my work is remote.
					Bangkok is six or seven hours ahead of London, so my afternoon is your
					morning. Australia and Singapore are close enough that it barely
					comes up. If you are in the Americas, we pick one time each week
					that suits us both and keep to it.
				</p>
				{/* The owner's working-style promise: he keeps Bangkok hours, but
				    reporting happens on the client's clock. Merged into the
				    scope-and-visibility paragraph, since they are the same idea
				    seen from two angles. */}
				<p>
					Honestly, the time difference is rarely what makes remote work
					difficult. I keep my own hours here, but I report progress at
					whatever time works for you, wherever you are. Beyond that, what
					really helps is agreeing the scope in writing and letting you watch
					the work take shape, so you are never left wondering where things
					stand. That is how I work with everyone, near or far.
				</p>
				<p>
					You will also be dealing with me directly, rather than an account
					manager relaying messages back and forth. When something is unclear,
					you can ask the person who actually wrote the code.
				</p>
				<p>
					And if your project touches Thailand at all, working in both
					languages saves a great deal of back and forth. I have built sites
					and systems that run in more than one language before, so it is
					familiar territory rather than something we would be figuring out
					together as we go.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-head reveal">
				<p class="label">The facts</p>
				<h2>Everything on one page</h2>
			</div>

			<dl class="facts reveal">
				{
					facts.map((f) => (
						<div class="fact">
							<dt>{f.label}</dt>
							<dd>{f.value}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>

			<div class="services reveal reveal-d1">
				<h3>What I take on</h3>
				<ul>
					{
						services.map((sv) => (
							<li>
								<a href={sv.href}>{sv.label}</a>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="channels reveal reveal-d2">
				<h3>How to reach me</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Email <a href={EMAIL_URL}>{EMAIL}</a>. I read and answer every one
						myself.
					</li>
					<li>
						If you are already in Thailand and prefer a chat app, that option
						is on the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						Code samples are on <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>GitHub</a
						>.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band">
		<div class="shell band-inner reveal">
			<p class="label">Get in touch</p>
			<h2>Not sure whether I can help? Just ask.</h2>
			<p class="lede">
				Tell me what your business does and what is getting in the way. I will
				let you know where I would start, and if I am not the right person for
				it, I will say so.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<MailButton label={`Email ${EMAIL}`} tone="on-dark" />
				<a class="cta-quiet" href="/en/work/">
					See the work
					<Icon name="arrow" size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.entity {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		max-width: 38rem;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
	}

	.page-head .lede strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.intro {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.intro-media,
	.intro-text {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.photo-frame {
		position: relative;
		max-width: 20rem;
	}

	.photo-frame::before {
		content: "";
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		transform: translate(0.75rem, 0.75rem);
		border: 1.5px solid var(--honey);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		opacity: 0.4;
		pointer-events: none;
	}

	.photo-frame :global(.ph) {
		position: relative;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	.intro-text {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-content: center;
	}

	.intro-text h2 {
		font-size: var(--fs-h2);
	}

	.intro-text p {
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 38rem;
	}

	.intro-text strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.intro {
			grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
			gap: 3rem;
			align-items: center;
		}
	}

	.why {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.why p {
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 38rem;
	}

	.facts {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0;
		margin: 0;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.fact {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.125rem 1.5rem;
		padding: 0.875rem 1.25rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.fact:first-child {
		border-top: 0;
	}

	.facts dt {
		font-family: var(--font-head);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: var(--fs-label);
		color: var(--honey-ink);
	}

	.facts dd {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
		min-width: 0;
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.fact {
			grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr);
			align-items: baseline;
			padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
		}
	}

	.services,
	.channels {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.625rem;
	}

	.services h3,
	.channels h3 {
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.services ul,
	.channels ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.4375rem;
	}

	.services li,
	.channels li {
		font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
		color: var(--muted);
		min-width: 0;
	}
</style>
